  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 141 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nAnother cool day is prevailing today as a surface ridge axis resides \nover the eastern CWA providing for weak mixing. This will aid in \nholding highs in the mid 40s to near 50. The surface ridge axis will \nslowly slide east of the CWA tonight however, winds will generally \nremain light under filtered high clouds allowing low to fall back \ninto the mid 20s to near 30. Tomorrow, northerly flow aloft relaxes \nas the surface ridge slides east of the area and weak WAA gets \nunderway. This will allow highs to rise into low to mid 50s. Monday, \nupper level ridging will build over the central CONUS in response to \na upper level trough digging into the west coast. This coupled with \ncontinued weak WAA will lift highs into the mid 50s to near 60.\n\nThe warming trend that begins today will continue through mid-week \nas Tuesday the upper level ridge axis builds directly over the area \nwith modest WAA getting underway. This will raise highs into the mid \n50s to lower 60s. On Wednesday, the aforementioned upper level west \ncoast trough will be moving through the Plains states with an \nattendant Pacific front also moving through the Plains. Strong WAA \nout ahead of the front with provide a breezy but mild day with highs \nin the 60s. Wednesday night a weakened upper level trough will move \nthrough the region pushing a weak front through the forecast area. \nMoisture will be very meager out ahead of this front however, a few \nwidely scattered light showers will be possible. Thursday, zonal \nflow aloft coupled with surface high pressure will keep highs held \nin the 60s. Thursday into Friday a upper level trough will quickly \nmove from the west coast into the eastern Rockies. This will push an \nattendant surface cold front into the western Plains on Friday. \nAnother day of strong WAA out ahead of this front on Friday will \ndrive highs into the mid 60s to lower 70s. Friday night into \nSaturday, the cold will move through the area providing the chance \nfor scattered showers and thunderstorms.",
